entries.def:
ἤ, 
disjunctive and comparative particle (Bl., §36, 12; 77, 11); 
__1. disjunctive, or; 
__(a) between single words: Mat.5.17 Mrk.6.56, Luk.2.24, Jhn.6.19, Rom.1.21, al.; 
__(b) before a sentence expressing a variation, denial or refutation of a previous statement, frequently in interrog. form: Mat.7.4, 9 Mrk.12.14, Luk.13.4, Rom.3.29; 6.3; 9.21, 1Co.6.9, 16 9:6, 2Co.11.7 ἤ . . . ἤ, either . . . or, Mat.6.24,…

ἦ (μήν), see: εἰ, iii, 7.
εἰ, 
conjunctive particle, used in conditions and in indirect questions. 
__I. Conditional, if; 
__1. with indic, expressing a general assumption; 
__(a) pres.: before indic, pres., Mat.11.14, Rom.8.25, al.; before imperat., Mrk.4.23; 9.22, Jhn.15.18, 1Co.7.9, al.; before fut. indic., Luk.16.31, Rom.8.11, al.; before pf. or aor., with negation in apodosis, Mat.12.26, Rom.4.14, al.;…
